{"request":{"path":"/rest/contents/search","query":{"limit":3,"offset":0,"projection":"full","sort":"viewsCount:desc"},"body":{"operator":"and","filters":{"format":{"includes":["video"]},"publishedAt":{"after":"2026-06-27","before":"2026-09-27"},"visualSimilarity":{"includes":{"values":[{"assetId":"ast_qwy2ywKE247as5SdhJk9QfFTmxfW","minScore":0.8}]}}},"queries":[{"operator":"or","filters":{"caption":{"includesExactly":{"values":["restaurant","restaurants"],"operator":"or"}}}},{"operator":"or","filters":{"caption":{"includesExactly":{"values":["dubai"],"operator":"or"}}}}]}},"status":200,"fetchedAt":"2026-09-27T10:25:49.379Z","response":{"data":{"aggregations":{"totalViewsCount":39184,"totalInteractionsCount":1173,"totalEngagementRatePerViews":0.029935688035933033,"totalEngagementRatePerFollowers":0.02150360226585272},"results":[{"id":"cnt_be4b0b8526e581d846d6b0f3268b","matchedQueries":[],"platform":"instagram","profileHandle":"tatlerdiningph","profileDisplayName":"Tatler Dining Philippines","format":"video","caption":"There’s a new Japanese restaurant in town—meet @hinoki.mnl 🍣🥢 \n\nThe more seasoned foodies among us may recall a kaiseki-style restaurant in Makati City by the name of Sushi Kappo Kobikicho. Open sometime between 2005 and 2011, the kappou was helmed by one chef Hino Yusuke—a chef that the Recto family had grown fond of, and maintained a relationship with even after the closure of his restaurant.\n\nOne may also recognise Hino for his stint at Edsa Shangri-La, where he led Senju as its master chef before pursuing other opportunities in Japan and Dubai.\n\nBut eventually, something called him back to Manila. When the Recto family (also partners at Asian-European favourite M Dining) set their intentions to open a Japanese restaurant, they knew Hino was the man for the job. And thus, Hinoki was born. \n\nOpened just this month, the restaurant offers both a chef’s counter omakase and à la carte dining, granting guests the flexibility to dine as they please. This philosophy extends to the beverage programme, offering a generous selection of wines by the glass and sake carafes, as well as the interiors by Studio Ong (@studio_ong), with three private rooms for those who seek it.\n\nWhich dishes are you most excited to try? Let us know in the comments below 💬\n\nEdited by: Dan Pablo\n\n#TatlerDiningPH #TatlerFirstLook","captionLanguage":"en","thumbnailMediaId":"med_624490bf2ab00ea6e535f4da6bea","publishedAt":"2026-07-13T08:19:13.000Z","profileId":"prf_00c2cdfeaa13682276628a92b5f5","thumbnailMediaUrl":"https://oriane-contents.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/Daud99BSc_I/thumbnail.webp","viewsCount":39184,"likesCount":522,"sharesCount":645,"commentsCount":6,"interactionsCount":1173,"engagementRatePerViews":2.9935688035933032,"engagementRatePerFollowers":2.150360226585272,"profileFollowersCount":54549,"profileFollowingCount":2136,"profilePostsCount":3434,"mediaCount":1,"duration":60.06,"hashtags":["#tatlerdiningph","#tatlerfirstlook"],"coAuthors":[{"id":null,"platformId":null,"profileHandle":"laurengolangco"},{"id":null,"platformId":null,"profileHandle":"studio_ong"},{"id":"prf_6ffa45bdcf5086b3faa7cd136c46","platformId":"248570982","profileHandle":"tatlerphilippines"},{"id":null,"platformId":null,"profileHandle":"roameats"}],"mentions":[{"id":null,"platformId":null,"profileHandle":"studio_ong"},{"id":null,"platformId":null,"profileHandle":"hinoki.mnl"}],"platformId":"Daud99BSc_I","profilePlatformId":"491134592","profilePictureUrl":"https://oriane-handles.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/tatlerdiningph/pfp.webp","profileBio":"Bite-sized updates from the @tatlerphilippines team. Watch this space for the best dining news🍴🥂","profileVerified":false,"locationPlatformId":"467871013546171","locationCompleteAddress":"Makati City","locationLatitude":14.576015,"locationLongitude":121.0141,"profileLocationPlatformId":null,"profileLocationCompleteAddress":null,"profileLocationLatitude":null,"profileLocationLongitude":null,"transcript":"Tell us about Hinoki. Hinoki is a sushi and omakase Japanese restaurant. Chef Hino, he spent some time in Japan, went to Dubai, and when he decided that he wanted to look for something new, we spoke to him and we decided to try this whole thing together. What are the signature dishes at Hinoki? I'd say most of our signature dishes are featured throughout our omakase. The king crab risotto and on the a la carte side, I'd say the unagi is a crowd favorite. Tell us a bit about the beverage program. We definitely wanted to offer a full range of wines by the glass and sake parac. They can come to Hinoki without ordering a full bottle. Can you tell us a little bit about the design of the restaurant? We spoke with Studio Ong. We wanted to find a balance between modern and authentic. Why did you want to open a Japanese restaurant? We really love Japanese food, so when we were given the opportunity, we thought that we had to jump on, and it's something we're all very excited for everyone to try. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited. We're all very excited.","transcriptLanguage":"en","transcriptChunks":[{"startSeconds":0.165,"endSeconds":1.725,"text":"Tell us about Hinoki."},{"startSeconds":1.725,"endSeconds":6.165,"text":"Hinoki is a sushi and omakase Japanese restaurant."},{"startSeconds":6.165,"endSeconds":9.445,"text":"Chef Hino, he spent some time in Japan, went to Dubai,"},{"startSeconds":9.445,"endSeconds":12.605,"text":"and when he decided that he wanted to look for something new,"},{"startSeconds":12.605,"endSeconds":16.285,"text":"we spoke to him and we decided to try this whole thing together."},{"startSeconds":16.285,"endSeconds":18.405,"text":"What are the signature dishes at Hinoki?"},{"startSeconds":18.405,"endSeconds":21.925,"text":"I'd say most of our signature dishes are featured throughout our omakase."},{"startSeconds":21.925,"endSeconds":24.645,"text":"The king crab risotto and on the a la carte side,"},{"startSeconds":24.645,"endSeconds":27.445,"text":"I'd say the unagi is a crowd favorite."},{"startSeconds":27.445,"endSeconds":29.045,"text":"Tell us a bit about the beverage program."},{"startSeconds":29.045,"endSeconds":32.485,"text":"We definitely wanted to offer a full range of wines by the glass"},{"startSeconds":32.485,"endSeconds":34.085,"text":"and sake parac."},{"startSeconds":34.085,"endSeconds":36.725,"text":"They can come to Hinoki without ordering a full bottle."},{"startSeconds":36.725,"endSeconds":39.285,"text":"Can you tell us a little bit about the design of the restaurant?"},{"startSeconds":39.285,"endSeconds":42.085,"text":"We spoke with Studio Ong."},{"startSeconds":42.085,"endSeconds":46.085,"text":"We wanted to find a balance between modern and authentic."},{"startSeconds":46.085,"endSeconds":48.165,"text":"Why did you want to open a Japanese restaurant?"},{"startSeconds":48.165,"endSeconds":49.845,"text":"We really love Japanese food,"},{"startSeconds":49.845,"endSeconds":52.005,"text":"so when we were given the opportunity,"},{"startSeconds":52.005,"endSeconds":54.085,"text":"we thought that we had to jump on,"},{"startSeconds":54.085,"endSeconds":57.845,"text":"and it's something we're all very excited for everyone to try."},{"startSeconds":59.045,"endSeconds":60.485,"text":"We're all very excited."},{"startSeconds":60.485,"endSeconds":62.485,"text":"We're all very excited."},{"startSeconds":62.485,"endSeconds":64.485,"text":"We're all very excited."},{"startSeconds":64.485,"endSeconds":66.485,"text":"We're all very excited."